window.STORY_CHAPTERS = [{"title":"The Girl Who Caught My Attention ❤️","subtitle":"How one Instagram request became the start of us","paragraphs":["It all began during the last year of my college, somewhere around April.","I still remember the first time I texted her on Instagram. Actually, I had heard about her from someone—if I remember correctly, it was my school friend, Anshuman. After hearing about her, I tried searching for her on Instagram, and eventually, I found her profile in my suggestions.","And there she was: Gyanvee.","I spent quite some time thinking about whether I should send her a follow request. It might sound like a small thing now, but back then, it felt like a big decision. I kept wondering, Should I send her a request? What would she think of me? Would she accept it? What if she thought I was being weird?","My mind was full of questions, and I was caught in a dilemma. But after all that overthinking, I finally gathered the courage to send her a request.","Honestly, I wasn't expecting much. In fact, I thought she probably wouldn't accept it.","But boom! 💥","Within a day, she accepted my request!","You have no idea how happy I was. It was such a small thing, yet it was enough to put a huge smile on my face. And just like that, my next mission began.","Should I text her?","That question started another round of overthinking. If I did text her, what should I say? How should I start the conversation? I wanted to message her, but I also didn't want to sound creepy or make a bad first impression.","I spent almost three days thinking about one simple message. 😂 One of my college friends even encouraged me to text her, probably getting tired of watching me overthink the same thing again and again.","And finally, I did it.","I sent her a message, secretly expecting that she might not reply at all—or that she might take a long time to respond. Maybe she would ignore me. Maybe she wouldn't be interested in talking to me.","But when she replied, I was so excited that I can't even explain it properly.","After getting placed, this became the second happiest day of my entire college life. And the funny part? My first message to her was:","\"Hey Gyanvee, do you know me?\" 😂","Now, when I think about it, how creepy was that opening line!","But her reply surprised me even more.","She said that she knew me because I had been the topper of our school.","Wait… what?","I had been prepared to introduce myself properly, explain that we had been in the same school batch, and remind her who I was. Instead, she already knew me!","I had spent so much time worrying about whether she would even recognize me, and there she was, remembering me as the school topper. 😄","We had a really good conversation that day. For me, it was the beginning of something exciting. I wanted to talk to her more, get to know her better, and somehow find a way to make talking to her a part of my everyday life.","But then came the next challenge.","How do you start a conversation with someone every day without making it seem like you're trying too hard?","I didn't know the answer. I just knew that I wanted to talk to her.","However, as time passed, her replies started getting slower. And naturally, my overthinking returned.","I began wondering whether she was getting frustrated with my messages or whether she simply didn't want to talk to me. I didn't want to bother her, so I gradually stopped texting her first.","Still, I couldn't completely stop myself from finding little ways to interact with her. Sometimes, I would send her a reel on Instagram. It wasn't very often, but whenever I did, a small part of me hoped that it might turn into a conversation.","Sometimes, she would react to the reel, and that would be it.","And honestly, I wanted more than just a reaction.","I wanted a reply. A conversation. Maybe even a reason to keep talking to her.","It might sound silly, but when you're waiting for a little interaction from someone you like, even the smallest things begin to matter. A simple reply can make your day, while a reaction without a conversation can leave you wondering what went wrong.","I didn't know what she was thinking, and I didn't want to assume too much. But from my side, I was slowly becoming disappointed.","Then, one day, I saw some kissing and love emojis on her Instagram story.","My mind immediately jumped to a conclusion: Maybe she's already committed to someone.","I didn't know for sure, but that one thought was enough to make me step back. I promised myself that I wouldn't text her again.","Maybe it was my way of protecting myself from disappointment. Maybe I thought that if I stopped expecting anything, I wouldn't keep getting hurt by the same little things.","But feelings don't always listen to the promises we make to ourselves, do they?","Even after deciding not to text her again, a part of me still wanted to talk to her.","And so, in December 2025, I messaged her again.","She replied, and we had another good conversation. For a little while, that familiar happiness returned. It felt like perhaps we could talk again, just like we had during our first conversation.","Somewhere in my heart, I think I was holding on to one last hope.","But once again, her replies were slow.","And once again, I started thinking that perhaps she wasn't really interested in continuing the conversation. I didn't want to force anything or make her uncomfortable, so I decided to step back.","This time, I told myself that I should move on and stop expecting any further interaction.","And that was where things stood.","Back then, I had no idea what the future held. I didn't know whether we would ever talk again, whether she would become someone important in my life, or whether these little Instagram conversations would eventually become nothing more than distant memories.","All I knew was that a girl I had once spent three days gathering the courage to text had somehow managed to occupy a little corner of my mind.","I thought that perhaps this was where my story with her would end.","But sometimes, the moments we think are the end of a story are only the beginning of something we cannot yet imagine. ❤️"]},{"title":"The Day She Texted First ❤️🌹","subtitle":"February 14, a flower, and our first call","paragraphs":["14th February. Saturday. Valentine's Day.","I was sleeping in the afternoon when suddenly, a reel popped up on my phone.","It was from Gyanvee.","For a moment, I couldn't believe what I was seeing. Gyanvee had sent me a reel, and the most special part was that she had texted me first, on her own.","You might think it was just a reel. Just a small message on Instagram. But for me, it was something much bigger than that.","My heartbeat started racing. I don't think I can properly explain that feeling to anyone—not even to you, Gyanvee. You have no idea how happy I was that day. Maybe, if you could have seen my face at that moment, you would have understood how much one little notification meant to me. ❤️","I opened the reel. It was about people waking up on Valentine's Day to roses and wishes from their loved ones, while the person in the reel woke up to a phone charged to 100%.","I smiled while watching it, but my mind was already busy with another question.","What should I reply?","I thought about it so much, as if I had to write the perfect response to the most important message of my life. 😂 And after all that thinking, guess what I did?","I simply reacted to the reel. 🥲","Yes, that's right. The boy who had spent days thinking about how to start a conversation had finally received a message from the girl herself, and all he could manage was a reaction!","But luckily, the universe—or maybe just my Instagram feed—had something better planned.","Soon, I came across another reel. This one had a cute little cat holding a flower. I immediately thought of sending it to her.","And so I sent it with a little message:","\"Aapke liye pyaara sa fool.\" 🌷❤️","Yes, fool instead of phool. 😂","Looking back, I don't know whether I was trying to be romantic or simply being myself. But that little message became the beginning of something beautiful.","That was the day our chapter truly began.","We started talking, and before we knew it, more than three hours had passed. Three hours! The same two people who had once barely managed to have a conversation were now talking as if we had so much to catch up on.","And honestly, I didn't want those conversations to end.","Three hours weren't enough. One day wasn't enough. I wanted more conversations, more time, more of her.","Over the next three days, we talked a lot. And with every conversation, I found myself wanting to know her a little more.","But there was one problem.","I wanted to hear her voice.","Typing messages was nice, but I wanted something more. I wanted to talk to her on a call, hear her laugh, listen to her stories, and experience what it felt like to have an actual conversation with her.","Of course, I couldn't just ask directly. That would have been too easy for someone like me. 😂","So I started making excuses.","\"Yaar, typing karte karte ungliyan dard karne lagti hain. Kuch aur tarika dhoondhna chahiye.\" ☺️","I brought up the idea for two days, hoping she would understand what I was trying to say. Maybe I thought she would eventually suggest a call herself, saving me from the embarrassment of asking directly.","And then, finally, she said something that I still remember:","\"Agar number chahiye toh bol do, itna kya makkar kar rahe ho?\" 😄","I swear, at that moment, I must have been smiling like an idiot at my phone.","All that overthinking, all those excuses, and she had figured it out!","Finally, she sent me her number, and I called her.","And then came a moment I had been waiting for.","The first time I heard her voice.","I had imagined talking to her so many times, but when the moment actually arrived, I went completely blank. I was almost numb. I was trying my best to act normal, pretending that I was comfortable and that talking to her was no big deal.","But Gyanvee understood me better than I expected.","She could tell that I was nervous, and then she said:","\"Lambi-lambi saansein lo.\" 😂❤️","Just imagine the situation. I had finally managed to call the girl I wanted to talk to so badly, and instead of being the smooth, confident guy I had imagined myself to be, I needed instructions on how to breathe!","But honestly, that moment was special. It was awkward, funny, and a little embarrassing, but it was ours.","And just like that, a new journey began.","We started talking on calls, and those calls slowly became a part of our lives. Sometimes, we would talk until four in the morning.","She would sit on the terrace because of her roommate, and I would sit in my balcony with a proper chair, ready for our long conversations. 😂","Two different places, two different settings, but somehow, we managed to create our own little world over the phone.","The rest of the world could sleep. We still had things to talk about.","And somewhere between those late-night calls, I began to change in ways I hadn't expected.","My Instagram feed, which had once been full of comedy and action content, suddenly started filling up with romantic songs. I would listen to those songs and imagine her.","A song would play, and my mind would create little scenes with her. Sometimes, I didn't even need a reason to think about her; the songs did the job for me.","A boy whose feed was once full of comedy and action had suddenly entered his full-on lovey-dovey era. 😂❤️","I don't know exactly when it happened, but somewhere along the way, talking to her stopped being just something that made me happy. It became something I looked forward to every single day.","Of course, our story wasn't going to be all sweet conversations and romantic songs. There were little insecurities, too.","And one of them had a name: Ariba. 😂","In the beginning, I wasn't particularly happy with Gyanvee's friendship with Ariba. I used to think that maybe, because of her, Gyanvee wouldn't become as close to me as I wanted her to.","Now, when I think about it, I can see how silly some of those thoughts were. But back then, I was inexperienced with these feelings. I didn't always know how to handle them.","Sometimes, when I called Gyanvee, she would joke around with Ariba, and I would get a little jealous. I didn't always know how to express that feeling properly.","And then, one day, I made another mistake.","I appreciated another girl in front of my baby, and Gyanvee became angry.","Perhaps I was acting out of my own frustration, or perhaps I didn't fully understand how my words might make her feel. Whatever the reason, she was upset, and I had to face the consequences of my actions.","During that moment, Ariba said something to me that felt awkward. My first thought was, Who is she to tell me off?","But then I stopped and thought about it.","Maybe she was only trying to stand up for Gyanvee because she cared about her. And if someone cared enough about my girl to look out for her, perhaps that wasn't such a bad thing after all.","I decided not to take it to heart.","And, of course, I had to make things right with my baby.","I said sorry to my kuchu puchu. ❤️","That was our first little fight.","It wasn't a huge argument, but it was one of those moments that taught me something about us. When two people start becoming important to each other, even small things can lead to misunderstandings.","And maybe that's part of getting to know each other, too.","Because love isn't always about romantic songs, long calls, and sweet words. Sometimes, it's about misunderstandings, apologies, and learning how to care for each other's feelings a little better.","Meanwhile, I had another mission going on in my life.","I wanted to finish my work as quickly as possible so that I could spend more time with my Gyanvee. The faster I finished everything, the sooner I could talk to her.","She had become one of the best parts of my day, and I wanted as much time with her as I could get.","But then, one day, my friends came to Pune to meet me, and I spent some time away from my usual routine with her.","That was when something happened that I still remember.","Gyanvee told me that if I didn't call her at midnight, it wouldn't be good.","It might sound like a small thing, but for me, it was special.","Until then, I had been the one trying to find excuses to talk to her, the one waiting for her messages, and the one hoping she would make time for me.","But that day, she was expecting something from me.","For the first time, I felt that she wanted something from me, too. She wanted me to call her at a particular time, and I wasn't going to let that moment pass.","So, at midnight, I called her.","And she was happy.","Maybe I was happy for an even bigger reason. It wasn't only about making a midnight call. It was about feeling that she wanted me there, too.","That feeling was new to me, and I loved it. ❤️","But as the days passed, another side of me started to appear.","My insecurities.","For a few days, Gyanvee was at home, and we didn't talk as much. I missed her, and I found myself feeling sad during the time we weren't talking.","I kept waiting for her to return to college, thinking that once she was back, things would become normal again.","And when she finally returned, I tried calling her.","But she was busy.","I texted her, but there was no reply. Two hours passed, and I still hadn't heard from her. I tried calling again, but she was still busy.","And slowly, my mind began creating stories of its own.","Why isn't she replying? Is something wrong? Does she not want to talk to me anymore? Have I done something?","I didn't have any answers, but my thoughts kept getting louder.","That night, I couldn't sleep properly. I kept looking at my phone again and again, hoping to see her name appear on the screen.","Every time I checked and found nothing, I felt a little more worried.","I wasn't angry. I was scared.","Scared that something had changed. Scared that the conversations I had started looking forward to every day might somehow disappear.","The next morning, I called her again.","And, with all those thoughts still running through my mind, I finally said something along the lines of:","\"Yaar, agar tumhe mujhse baat nahi karni, toh please bata do. Koi baat nahi, nahi karenge.\"","I think I was trying to prepare myself for the worst before I even knew what was happening.","And then she explained.","\"Yaar, bhaiya toh bas suna rahe the.\" 🥲","That was it.","She had been busy because her brother was scolding her, and here I was, spending an entire night worrying about what her silence meant!","When I understood what had actually happened, I felt relieved. All those thoughts, all that fear, all that unnecessary overthinking—and the answer had been much simpler than I had imagined.","After that, things became normal again.","Our conversations started flowing like before, and we were happy again.","Looking back, I can laugh at some of these moments. The nervous first call, the romantic reels, my jealousy over Ariba, the midnight call, and the night I couldn't sleep because she hadn't replied.","But these little moments mean something to me.","They remind me of the boy I was at the beginning of our story: someone who overthought a simple message, who became nervous just hearing her voice, who waited for her replies, and who slowly began to understand what it meant to have someone become so important.","I didn't know everything about love back then. I was learning as I went along, sometimes getting things right and sometimes letting my insecurities get the better of me.","But one thing was certain.","I wanted to talk to her again the next day.","And the day after that.","And every day that I could.","Because somewhere between that Valentine's Day reel and those late-night calls, Gyanvee had become more than just the girl I had once been too nervous to text. She had become the girl whose voice could calm me, whose messages could make my day, and whose presence I had started missing even before she was gone.","And this was only the beginning of us. ❤️"]},{"title":"April — The Meeting That Never Happened ❤️🥹","subtitle":"The April meeting that almost happened","paragraphs":["April had arrived, and with it came a new hope.","Maybe, just maybe, I was finally going to meet my Gyanvee.","Our relationship was long-distance. She was living in Gonda, Uttar Pradesh, while I was working in Pune. She was studying at UPUMS in Etawah, and although Gonda was our hometown, our lives were taking place in different cities.","The distance between us wasn't just about kilometres. It was about wanting to see someone and not being able to, about hearing her voice every night but still wishing I could sit beside her, and about imagining the moment when I would finally get to see her in person.","Until then, our relationship had been built through messages, reels, and those endless late-night calls. I knew her voice, her habits, her little moods, and the way she could make me smile even when she wasn't physically around.","But now, I wanted something more.","I wanted to meet her.","There was just one problem: Gyanvee kept saying that she didn't want to meet me. 😂","Even when we talked about meeting, she would insist that she wasn't calling me to Etawah. Sometimes, she would say that if I really wanted to meet her, I should come all the way from Pune just for her.","At first, I couldn't understand her.","Deep down, I felt that she wanted to meet me, too. Maybe she was shy, maybe she was hesitant, or maybe there was something else on her mind. I couldn't know for sure.","But I kept hoping.","Around 28th April, my elder sister's wedding was scheduled, and I was going to my hometown for it. Since Gyanvee's college was in Etawah, I thought this would be the perfect opportunity to meet her after the wedding.","For me, it seemed like everything was finally falling into place.","I was already going home. She was relatively nearby. All we needed was the right time.","But whenever I brought up the idea, she would repeat the same thing: if I wanted to meet her, I should come to Etawah specifically for her, not because I was already coming home.","Slowly, I began to wonder whether she really wanted to meet me at all.","I felt confused. One moment, I was imagining our first meeting, and the next, I was questioning whether it would ever happen.","What I didn't fully understand at the time was how difficult things were for her.","She had internal examinations, practicals, and internships to manage. Her schedule was already exhausting, and meeting me would mean finding time in the middle of all those responsibilities.","Looking back, I realise that I was so caught up in the excitement of meeting her that I wasn't always able to see the pressure she was under.","And yet, even with everything going on, she still made time for me.","I remember her internship days. She would leave around nine in the morning and return at around five in the evening. After spending the entire day at college and doing her internship, she would still talk to me until three or four in the morning.","Just think about it.","A whole day of work, barely enough rest, and then hours of talking to me late into the night.","How cute was my baby? 🥹❤️","Sometimes, I wonder how she managed to do it. She had so much going on in her life, yet she would still find time for our conversations.","And one day, because of incomplete sleep, she fainted in the lab.","I felt bad thinking about how exhausted she must have been. I never wanted my baby to feel so tired, especially when she already had so much to handle.","She would tell me stories about her professors, too, especially about the creepy behaviour some of them showed towards girls.","She once told me about a professor who tried to hold her hand while teaching her how to draw blood for testing. She also talked about a professor who was around forty years old and behaved inappropriately.","Every time she told me these stories, I would feel angry on her behalf.","Seriously, what kind of behaviour was that? 😤","Some of those professors really sounded like characters nobody would want to encounter in real life.","And then there was Harsh.","She would sometimes tell me about a boy named Harsh who was trying very hard to get close to her. He would wait for her at the end of the day and offer to give her a ride to her hostel.","But she would refuse.","Instead, she would walk all the way to her hostel because she knew I might feel bad about it.","Whenever I thought about that, I felt a strange mixture of relief and affection. It meant a lot to me that she considered my feelings.","At the same time, I knew that she had her own life, her own challenges, and her own decisions to make. I didn't want her to feel that she had to make things difficult for herself just to reassure me.","April was a hard month for my Gyanvee.","Every day, we would talk about the same question.","\"Hum mil payenge na April ke end tak?\"","And her answer would often leave me disappointed.","She would explain that it was going to be difficult because her external examinations might take place around that time in May.","Every time she said that, my heart sank a little.","I knew she wasn't necessarily saying no forever. She had genuine responsibilities, and I understood that. But understanding something logically doesn't always stop you from feeling sad about it.","I kept imagining what it would be like to meet her. What would I say when I saw her? Would I be nervous the same way I had been during our first call? Would I go completely blank again?","I had so many little thoughts about that moment.","And the more I imagined it, the more I wanted it to happen.","But one day, something happened that made me realise I still had a lot to learn about being there for her.","She was feeling sad and started telling me about her father and her brother. Her father wasn't keeping well, and her brother was strict with her.","She was sharing her feelings with me, and I was listening.","But instead of simply understanding her emotions and comforting her, I started giving her advice.","I thought I was helping. I thought that if I explained things or offered solutions, she might feel better.","But later, I realised something important.","Sometimes, when a person opens their heart to you, they aren't asking you to solve their problems. They just want someone to listen, understand, and make them feel safe enough to express what they're going through.","They don't always need a lecture or an explanation.","Sometimes, they just need a little affection.","A little reassurance.","A little \"Babu, main hoon na. Tum tension mat lo.\"","That day taught me something about the kind of partner I wanted to become.","Gyanvee, I'm sorry for that day. ❤️","I'm sorry that when you needed comfort, I tried to give you advice instead. I was still learning how to understand your feelings, and I know that sometimes, caring about someone isn't enough if you don't know how to show that care in the way they need it.","I wanted to make you happy, but I was still learning how.","And I was learning from you, too.","Then came the day I finally arrived at my hometown for my elder sister's wedding.","The house was full of wedding preparations, relatives, conversations, laughter, and the usual chaos that comes with an Indian wedding.","But somewhere in the middle of all that, I had another little secret to look forward to.","Gyanvee.","I was still talking to her at night, and my family gradually started noticing that something was going on.","One of my favourite cousins began teasing me about her. Slowly, even my brother started suspecting something.","I became worried that they might tell my mother.","Imagine my situation. I had travelled home for my elder sister's wedding, but I was spending my nights talking to a girl and trying to make sure nobody found out! 😂","At one point, even my father told me to sleep with him, probably because he had noticed how late I was staying awake.","I started wondering whether my entire family had somehow figured out my little secret.","And then came one of the funniest moments.","One day, my cousin showed my mother Gyanvee's picture.","My mother apparently couldn't believe that her son could pull a girl like her.","And the reaction was something along the lines of:","\"Yeh toh langoor ke haath mein angoor!\" 😂","And honestly, I couldn't even argue with that.","Haan bhai, langoor toh main hi hoon! 😂❤️","But jokes aside, somewhere inside, I was proud of my girl. Even my family could see how beautiful she was.","And there I was, the same boy who had once spent three days thinking about whether to send her a message.","Who would have thought that one day, my family would be looking at her picture and teasing me about her?","Life really does have a funny way of changing things.","The wedding finally came and went. The celebrations ended, the relatives began returning to their homes, and my departure date started getting closer.","I had a flight back to Pune in four days.","Gyanvee still had her examinations, and by then, it was becoming clear that meeting her before I left might not be possible.","I felt disappointed.","I kept thinking about the decision I had made while booking my flight.","Why did I book my return flight for that day?","Maybe I should have stayed another four or five days. Maybe, if I had booked my flight later, we would have found a chance to meet.","I kept imagining an alternate version of April in which I stayed a little longer and finally got to see her.","But reality was different.","She had her examinations, and I didn't want her to feel pressured to meet me in the middle of such an important and hectic period. Even though she had said that she would meet me, I knew that it could be exhausting for her to manage everything at once.","I wanted to meet her more than I could explain.","But I also wanted her to be okay.","I didn't want our first meeting to become another responsibility on her already long list of things to do.","So I returned to Pune.","Without meeting her.","And honestly, it hurt.","After all those conversations, all those plans, all that excitement, I was going back to the same city where I had been before, carrying nothing from that trip except memories of the days we had spent talking from a distance.","I had gone home hoping that April would finally bring us closer.","But April ended without giving me the moment I had been waiting for.","I was disappointed in myself. I kept wondering whether I should have planned things differently, whether I should have stayed longer, whether I had missed an opportunity that might not come again anytime soon.","But there was one thing I knew.","I didn't regret putting her examinations first.","Because I didn't just want to meet her. I wanted her to be happy, too.","And if waiting a little longer meant that she could focus on her studies without carrying the additional pressure of meeting me, then I could wait.","Still, somewhere in my heart, I carried a small wish.","The wish to see her standing in front of me one day, no longer just a face on my phone or a voice coming through my earphones.","The wish to finally look at her and think, So this is the girl I've spent so many nights talking to.","April didn't give me our first meeting.","But it gave me more memories of her: her late-night conversations despite her exhausting schedule, her stories about college, her little ways of considering my feelings, and the lessons I was slowly learning about loving someone.","And perhaps, without even realising it, I was learning that love wasn't only about how desperately you wanted to be with someone.","Sometimes, it was also about understanding when to wait.","I returned to Pune without meeting my Gyanvee. But my story with her was far from over. ❤️"]},{"title":"The Boy Was Finally Coming ❤️✈️","subtitle":"A journey from Pune to Etawah","paragraphs":["May had arrived, bringing with it long, hot days. But honestly, the heat outside was nothing compared to the excitement building inside me. 🥹❤️","Our conversations had started revolving around one question again and again…","“Hum milenge kab?”","When would we finally meet?","I was getting more excited with every passing day. Sometimes, I would seriously think about booking a flight to Delhi and then travelling from Delhi to Etawah just to see her. I had started imagining the entire journey in my head, thinking about where we would go, what we would do, and how it would feel to finally stand in front of the girl I had spent so many nights talking to.","But whenever I talked about my plans, she had one favourite dialogue.","“Koi jarurat nahi, tumhe koi bula nahi raha hai.” 😂❤️","She would say it in that naughty, teasing way of hers, as if she didn't want me to come at all.","But somewhere deep down, I felt that she wanted to meet me too. Maybe she was just as nervous as I was, or perhaps she had her own reasons for hiding her excitement behind those words. I couldn't be sure, but I loved teasing her about meeting.","Sometimes, my imagination would go a little too far. I would start discussing plans for a trip to Rishikesh or suggest that we could meet in Delhi instead.","And her answer?","A big, fat NO. 😂","The problem wasn't simply that she didn't want to go. Her brother was very particular about her whereabouts, and they both used the same Apple account on their phones. That meant he could check her location. Going somewhere without telling him was risky for her, and I gradually understood why she was so scared of leaving Etawah.","Still, the excited boy inside me didn't know how to stop making plans. I would bring up Delhi again and again, and sometimes she would get genuinely angry with me.","Then, like the obedient boyfriend I was trying to become, I would immediately surrender.","“Achha baba, theek hai. Delhi nahi jayenge. Etawah mein hi kahin mil lenge.” 🤭","But even that came with another problem.","She always told me that Etawah wasn't a good place to meet and that I wouldn't even find a decent room there.","I would confidently reply that I would manage somehow.","How difficult could it be? I thought.","Well, apparently, finding a good room in Etawah wasn't as easy as making romantic plans from Pune. 😂","I searched online, looked for suitable places, and tried to figure out where we could stay. I even contacted the brother of a friend who studied at the same college as her, hoping he might help me with some local information. Unfortunately, he was only in his first year and couldn't really provide the information I needed.","But I didn't want to depend entirely on anyone else. I wanted to figure things out myself.","The funny part? Gyanvee didn't even know how much effort I was putting into all this. I was secretly searching for rooms and making plans while, on the other side, she kept telling me not to come. 😂❤️","Nothing was final yet, but in my mind, the meeting had already started.","And then, one day, I got a little upset.","I felt that she didn't want me to come and meet her at all, so I said something along those lines to her.","And her reply was…","“Aur kaise bulau?” ☺️❤️","Just imagine that!","The same girl who kept saying, “Koi jarurat nahi, tumhe koi bula nahi raha,” was now asking me, “Aur kaise bulau?”","That one little line was enough to melt my heart.","I don't know whether she realised how cute she sounded at that moment, but I certainly did. Sometimes, she would tease me so much that I would start doubting everything, and then she would say one small thing that made me forget all my complaints.","That was Gyanvee.","And I was already hopelessly gone for her.",{"type":"heading","text":"The Hawasi Darinda & His Anvee 🤭❤️"},"Of course, May wasn't just about planning our first meeting.","It was also the month when our conversations grew longer, our comfort with each other increased, and we started talking about things we hadn't discussed so freely before. Some of our conversations became a little naughty, too. 😊","And let me tell you something: even though I was the one sometimes starting those conversations, I was also the one who got scared of my own words!","Whenever I wanted to say something a little naughty, I would first ask for permission.","“Can I say something?”",{"type":"heading","text":"And she would reply in her usual casual way,"},"“Hm hm, bolo.” 😅","Now, the funny thing was that even after getting permission, I would still be nervous.","I would think, What if she gets angry? What if she thinks I have a dirty mind? What if she calls me hawasi?","And guess what?","She eventually gave me a nickname that perfectly matched all my fears.","“Hawasi Darinda.” 😂😂❤️","Wow, Gyanvee. Just wow.","From being the boy who took three days to send you his first message to becoming your Hawasi Darinda—what a journey!","But I had a nickname for her, too.","I combined her name, Gyanvee, with Anugya, her name at home, and came up with…","Anvee. ❤️","It felt special because it was made from parts of her names. It was my own little name for her, something that belonged to our world.","Although, to be fair, she wasn't always impressed by it. She would say it sounded like a baby's nickname.","And honestly?","She wasn't wrong.","Because to me, she was my baby.","My baby. My cute girl. My Anvee. 🥹❤️","The girl who could tease me one moment, make me nervous the next, and still somehow make me smile at my phone like an idiot.","But there was another side to all this.","As much as I loved her playful side, I was slowly learning that when my baby was upset, it hurt me too. Whenever she became sad or angry, I would feel terrible. I wanted to make things better for her, but I didn't always know how.","And sometimes, that became my biggest mistake.",{"type":"heading","text":"When My Baby Needed Comfort, Not Advice 🥹"},"During this time, Gyanvee had a fight with two of her friends, Ariba and Ankit.","Ariba and Ankit had actually become friends because of Gyanvee. They had known each other through her, but now she found out that the two of them were bitching about her between themselves.","Think about how hurtful that must have felt.","Two people she considered her friends were talking about her behind her back. And to make it worse, they had become connected because of her in the first place.","She was hurt, and understandably so.","I wanted to help her. I wanted her to feel better. I wanted to fix whatever was making her sad.","But, unfortunately, I made the same mistake again.","Instead of comforting her the way she needed, I started giving her advice.","🥲","Yes, the classic mistake of a boy who thinks he can solve every problem with a few sensible words.","Sometimes, she didn't need me to explain what she should do. She didn't need a list of solutions or someone analysing the situation.","She needed her boyfriend.","She needed someone who would listen, understand her feelings, pamper her a little, and make her feel that she didn't have to handle everything alone.","She needed to be babied.","And I was busy giving advice.","No wonder she got even angrier. 🥲❤️","Looking back, I realise that loving someone isn't always about finding the right solution. Sometimes, it's about understanding what the other person needs from you in that moment.","Sometimes, the best response isn't advice.","It's simply, “Babu, I'm here. Tell me everything.”","Eventually, things settled between Gyanvee and Ariba, and they became happy together again. She reduced her interaction with Ankit, and things gradually became better.","I was happy that she wasn't carrying that hurt anymore.","But I was also learning something about myself: I still had a lot to learn about how to love her the way she wanted to be loved.","And I wanted to learn.","For her.",{"type":"heading","text":"The Ticket That Almost Ruined Everything 😭✈️"},"After so many discussions, so many plans, and so many versions of “we'll see,” the day finally came.","I booked my flight ticket to Delhi.","I was finally going to meet Gyanvee.","The girl I had first found on Instagram. The girl whose replies once made me overthink everything. The girl I had spent countless nights talking to. The girl who had become such an important part of my everyday life.","I was going to see her in real life.","For the first time.","I was beyond excited. I had imagined this moment so many times that it almost didn't feel real anymore.","But, of course, the universe—or perhaps my own carelessness—had to add some drama to the story. 😂","On the day of my flight, I made a mistake.","I thought my flight was at 11 p.m.","It was actually at 10 p.m.","And when did I realise this?","At 9 p.m.","ONE HOUR BEFORE THE FLIGHT.","My heart practically stopped.","For a moment, I couldn't think straight. All I could imagine was missing the flight, losing the chance to meet her, and watching the entire plan fall apart once again.","No. Not again.","I had already missed my chance to meet her in April. I had waited, planned, imagined, and finally booked this trip.","I wasn't going to let it fail now.","I forgot about booking an auto to the airport. Instead, I called my roommate, grabbed what I needed, and we jumped on his bike.","My heart was beating so fast that I could barely think about anything other than reaching the airport.","And then began one of the most stressful rides of my life.","I used every bit of my riding skill to get there on time. My roommate, meanwhile, was probably reconsidering every life decision that had led him to that moment. 😂","I was focused on one thing: reaching the airport.","He was probably focused on staying alive.","Honestly, I couldn't blame him. 🥲","When we finally reached the airport, I still wasn't safe.","I had to run approximately 600 metres with my trolley to reach the gate. I was sweating all over—not just because of the heat, but because of the nervousness, the panic, and the fear of missing my flight.","I must have looked like someone running for his life.","And, in a way, I was.","Because somewhere in my mind, this wasn't just another flight.","This flight was taking me to her. ❤️","I rushed inside, only to be told that boarding had already become an issue. I requested security to let me move ahead in the queue. They warned me that I was going to miss my flight.","But I kept trying.","I wasn't ready to give up.","And then, finally, I got lucky.","The flight was delayed by another thirty minutes.","Thirty minutes.","That little delay felt like a blessing sent specifically for one panicking, sweating, hopelessly-in-love boy.","I managed to board.","I had made it.","I was actually going to Delhi.","I was actually going to meet her.","After everything, the flight wasn't missed, the plan wasn't ruined, and my dream of meeting my baby was still alive. 😭❤️","Once I had a moment to breathe, I told Gyanvee the whole story.","Naturally, she scolded me.","And honestly, I deserved it. 😂","But beneath all that scolding, I could finally focus on the thought that had been running through my mind all day.","I was one step closer to her.",{"type":"heading","text":"Delhi Today, Etawah Tomorrow ❤️"},"I finally reached Delhi.","But my journey wasn't over yet.","The next day, I would head to Etawah, where Gyanvee was waiting—or at least, where I hoped she would be waiting for me. 🤭❤️","My excitement was impossible to explain.","I had spent so long imagining what it would be like to meet her that now, with the day finally approaching, I had started feeling nervous too.","What would happen when I saw her?","Would we talk normally, the way we did on calls?","Would I become awkward?","Would she?","Would I know what to say, or would every word disappear the moment I stood in front of her?","I had heard her voice countless times. I knew her laugh, her teasing, her little ways of making me nervous. I knew the girl who called me her Hawasi Darinda and the girl who rolled her eyes at my nickname for her.","But seeing someone through a phone screen and standing in front of them are two completely different things.","And tomorrow, I was finally going to discover that difference.","I was going to meet my baby for the very first time.","I don't know for certain how nervous she was. Maybe she was excited, maybe she was scared, or maybe she was simply trying not to show what she felt.","All I knew was what I felt.","For me, this meeting had become a dream—one I had thought about for days, made plans for, nearly ruined with my own mistake, and somehow managed to save at the last moment.","And now, finally, I was here.","Delhi was just a stop on my journey.","My destination was her. ❤️🥹","Tomorrow, the girl behind all those messages, calls, nicknames, fights, and late-night conversations would no longer be just a face on my phone.","Tomorrow, I would finally see my Gyanvee.","And the Kambakht Ladka who had been saying, “I just want to meet you,” was finally going to get his wish.","To be continued… ❤️🌹"]},{"title":"Finally, Face to Face ❤️🥹","subtitle":"Finally, face to face","paragraphs":[{"type":"heading","text":"The Countdown Was Finally Over ✈️❤️"},"The countdown had begun.","I was finally in Etawah, and I was just half an hour away from her.","After so many days of planning, countless conversations about when we would meet, and all those moments when she would tease me by saying, “Koi jarurat nahi, tumhe koi bula nahi raha,” I was finally there.","I had booked a room and taken an auto towards her college.","Now, one small detail about Etawah: finding an auto there wasn't the easiest task. 😂 But luckily, I managed to find one, and off I went towards the place where my baby was waiting.","Or, more accurately, the place where I hoped I would finally get to see my baby.","As the auto moved closer to her college, my heartbeat kept getting faster.","I was excited. I was nervous. I was happy.","And honestly, I was scared too.","Ten minutes before reaching the college, I called Gyanvee. She started making her way from her hostel towards the college gate.","And those last ten minutes felt like an eternity.","I had imagined this moment so many times. I had thought about what I would say, how I would greet her, and what I would do when I finally saw her.","In my imagination, everything was perfectly planned.","I would get out of the auto, hug her, and then ask her to sit inside.","Simple, right?","Well, real life had other plans. 😂",{"type":"heading","text":"The Boy Who Forgot How to Speak 🥲"},"Finally, we reached her college gate.","I saw her from a distance and asked the auto driver to stop in front of the girl standing there.","And there she was. My Gyanvee.","The girl whose face I had seen on my phone so many times was standing right in front of me.","My first instinct was to get out of the auto, hug her, and welcome her properly.","But the moment I saw her, my brain stopped working.","Completely.","I went blank.","All those plans I had made? Gone.","All those things I had imagined saying? Gone.","All the confidence I thought I would have? Nowhere to be found.",{"type":"heading","text":"I was about to get out when she said,"},"“Baitho, baitho. Mai aa jaungi.” 😂","And just like that, she sat beside me in the auto.","There I was, sitting next to the girl I had travelled all the way from Pune to meet, and I could barely look at her properly.","I wanted to see her. I wanted to take in that moment and remember every little detail.","But this was our first meeting, and I didn't have the courage to stare at her. I was too shy, too nervous, and too busy trying to act normal.","Before meeting her, I had imagined that she might be nervous too, and that I would have to start the conversation and make her comfortable.","But the opposite happened.","She was interacting normally, while I was struggling to remember how conversations worked. 🥲😂","I tried my best not to let my nervousness show. I wanted to create a good first impression, to start a conversation, to make the moment less awkward.","And then, in an attempt to create a topic, I said something I probably should have thought about twice.","“Baal toh tumhare fir rahe hai.” 😂🥲","Yes. That was one of my opening lines.","Imagine travelling all the way to meet the girl you like, dreaming about your first meeting, and then coming up with that.","I don't even know what was going through my mind. I was so nervous that I was saying whatever came to me.","I wanted to start a conversation, but instead, I created an awkward moment that I would probably remember for a long time.","Wah, Nikhil. Kya first impression banaya hai! 😂","Still, we slowly settled into the journey. She showed me the clock tower and the big Hanuman Ji idol as we travelled towards the room.","And even though I was nervous, I was happy.","Because she was right there.","For the first time, I didn't have to imagine what it would be like to sit beside her.","I was actually doing it.",{"type":"heading","text":"The Bouquet, The Gift & The First Hug 🌹🎁"},"After about half an hour, we reached the hotel.","I had already been worried about finding a decent room in Etawah, and now we were finally there. When we entered, the hotel manager gave me a look that made me feel as though he was judging us. Maybe it was just my imagination, but I noticed it immediately.","I was too excited to let it bother me for long.","There was something I had planned for her.","I had ordered a small bouquet through Blinkit. I wanted to give her flowers when we met, something cute that would make her smile.","Unfortunately, the bouquet wasn't quite as beautiful as I had imagined. 🥲😂","But there wasn't much I could do about that now.","When Gyanvee entered the room, I gave it to her.","And honestly, I felt a little embarrassed about the bouquet. I had wanted everything to be perfect, but the flowers weren't exactly helping my grand romantic plan.","Still, I hoped she would like the thought behind them.","Then I gave her another gift: a pair of studs.","And this time, I could see how happy she was.","That made me happy too. ❤️","Sometimes, you spend so much time thinking about what to give someone that you forget the best part is seeing their reaction when they receive it.","For me, her happiness was worth more than the gifts themselves.","But there was one more thing we hadn't done yet.","We hadn't hugged.","Before meeting, we had talked about hugging each other when we finally saw each other. Yet, even after arriving at the room, I was still too shy to bring it up properly.","Finally, I told her that she hadn't hugged me.","And she hugged me.","My first hug with Gyanvee. 🥹❤️","Except, if you ask me whether I hugged her properly, the answer is probably no.","I was so shy that I couldn't even manage that properly. 😂","I had travelled all that way, imagined the moment countless times, and then became a nervous little boy when it finally happened.","But that was me.","A boy who could make a hundred plans in his head but sometimes struggled to do the simplest things when his feelings were involved.","And that first hug?","It was one of the moments I had been waiting for.",{"type":"heading","text":"Breakfast, Cold Coffee & One Very Shy Boy ☕❤️"},"After that, we ordered breakfast.","I thought Gyanvee might like cold coffee, so we ordered it.","Unfortunately, the cold coffee wasn't very good. 😂","Apparently, even the smallest things weren't going to go exactly according to my plans that day.","At one point, she fed me the first bite.","And there I was again, feeling shy over the smallest gesture.","It was such a simple thing, but because it was happening with her, it felt different.","I had imagined spending time with her for so long that even ordinary moments felt special.","I had also thought about doing a few cute things myself, but whenever I considered actually doing them, I would become nervous and start overthinking.","Should I do it? What if it feels awkward? What if she doesn't like it?","And by the time I had finished asking myself all those questions, the moment would pass.","I sometimes wonder how much time I spent fighting with my own thoughts instead of simply enjoying being with her.","But then again, it was our first meeting.","I was learning how to be around her in real life, and she was no longer just a voice on a call or a face on my screen.","She was sitting right there, sharing breakfast with me.","And I was trying to remember how to act normal. 🥲❤️",{"type":"heading","text":"Fifty Shades of Grey & The Boy Who Fell Asleep 😂"},"After breakfast, I was lying on the bed while Gyanvee sat on a chair.","I told her she could sit on the bed and that I would take the chair instead.","But she told me that I didn't need to sit on the chair and could sit with her on the bed.","So we settled down and started deciding what to watch on television.","And then we remembered our old conversations about Fifty Shades of Grey.",{"type":"heading","text":"We had discussed that movie before meeting, and she used to say,"},"“Maine kahani dekhi hai bas uss movie ki.”",{"type":"heading","text":"And I would reply,"},"“Maine kahani skip ki hai.” 😂","So, naturally, we joked about watching it together and completing the story.","It was one of those silly little things that made our conversations feel like ours. We had talked about it before we met, and now we were sitting together, finally able to do something we had once discussed from a distance.","But then something completely unexpected happened.","I started feeling sleepy.","And eventually…","I fell asleep. 😂😂","Can you imagine?","Meeting your girlfriend for the very first time, spending all that time travelling to see her, finally getting to sit together—and then falling asleep!","I don't know what she was thinking at that moment, but I can imagine how strange it must have seemed.","We had been talking for two or three hours, and I had become so comfortable that I simply fell asleep.","I woke up after about an hour.","Looking back, it still makes me laugh. Our first meeting wasn't some perfectly scripted romantic movie. There were awkward lines, disappointing cold coffee, an imperfect bouquet, and a boyfriend who couldn't stay awake.","But those little imperfections were part of our real story too.",{"type":"heading","text":"The First Evening Together 🌙"},"We had talked before meeting about trying a drink together. She hadn't tried alcohol before, while I had started drinking back in my second year of college.","So we decided to have a drink.","As the evening went on, we both became intoxicated.","And this is where I need to be honest about something.","At one point, I asked her to kiss me. She said that we shouldn't do that, but I went ahead anyway.","I should have respected what she said.","Being excited, being in love, or being under the influence of alcohol doesn't give me the right to cross someone's boundary. I wish I had handled that moment differently.","I can't change what happened, but I can acknowledge that I was wrong.","I don't want to pretend that every moment of our first meeting was perfect, because it wasn't. I want this story to hold the truth of what happened, including the parts I regret.","Later, Gyanvee said she needed to return to her college. But it was already around 6 p.m., and with the college's entry restrictions after 7 p.m., we were worried she wouldn't make it back in time.","Ariba called her to check whether she was okay. I answered that she was okay, but Ariba wanted to hear confirmation from Gyanvee herself.","And that was completely understandable. She was Gyanvee's friend, and she wanted to know directly that her friend was safe.","Eventually, Gyanvee stayed.","We had dinner and watched a show together. Later, we spent time cuddling and kissing.","There were moments that felt comforting and precious to me, moments when I was simply happy to have her beside me after so many days of missing her.","But I also know that affection has to come with care, respect, and clear consent. I wish I had understood that better in every moment we shared.","That first night together became one of the most memorable nights of my life—but not every memory from it is a happy one for her.","And I cannot ignore that difference.",{"type":"heading","text":"When Ariba Joined Our Little World 😂❤️"},"The next day, Ariba came to meet us.","And the atmosphere changed completely.","Now it wasn't just the two of us. Ariba was there too, and the three of us spent time together, had drinks, and danced.","One thing I noticed was how confidently Gyanvee and Ariba handled themselves. They seemed so comfortable together that, at times, I wondered whether they had been drinking for years. 😂","At one point, I even found myself a little intimidated by Ariba.","She was abusing someone—if I remember correctly, it was Ankit—and the way she was going on about it was genuinely funny.","I couldn't help laughing.","Meanwhile, Gyanvee was looking after Ariba and making sure she was okay. My baby had her own way of caring for people, even while enjoying herself.","That was something I liked about her.","She could be playful and silly, but she also cared about her friends.","Later, we had dinner together. Ariba sat on one side, I sat on the other, and Gyanvee was between us.","I cuddled with Gyanvee for a while, but sometimes she became worried that Ariba might notice. Whenever she felt uncomfortable, I stopped.","At one point, I rested my face against her chest.","It felt peaceful to me.","After all the excitement, travelling, nervousness, and emotions of the past two days, being close to her felt comforting.","Eventually, we went to sleep.","And when morning arrived, Ariba started talking about returning and encouraged Gyanvee to go back to college too.","But I wasn't ready for our time together to end.","We had finally met after waiting so long, and now it felt as though the days were passing too quickly.","I wanted just one more day.","One more day with my baby.","And, thankfully, Gyanvee agreed to stay.",{"type":"heading","text":"One More Day, One More Night ❤️🥹"},"We spent another day together.","For me, it was difficult to think about leaving when I had only just got the chance to be with her. I wanted to make the most of the little time we had before I had to return to Pune.","That evening, we drank again.","Both of us became heavily intoxicated.","And that night, I did something that deeply hurt Gyanvee and damaged the trust she had placed in me.","I know what I did was wrong. I know that being drunk is not an excuse, and I won't use it to escape responsibility.","I can't describe the incident in detail here because I don't want to invent words for what happened or speak on Gyanvee's behalf about how she experienced it.","But I can say this: I regret hurting her, and I'm sorry for the trust I broke.","Gyanvee, if you're reading this, I know that saying sorry doesn't undo what happened. I know that promising to do better cannot erase the hurt you felt.","I wish that night had been different. I wish I had made better choices and protected the trust you had placed in me.","You came into that meeting with your own feelings, your own expectations, and your own trust in me. I should have treated all of that with the care it deserved.","I cannot rewrite that night into a beautiful memory simply because I wanted our first meeting to be perfect.","And I don't want to.","Some memories make us smile when we look back. Others remind us of the person we never want to be again.","This was a moment that forced me to look at myself honestly.","I'm sorry, Gyanvee.","Not because I want you to forget what happened, and not because I expect you to forgive me just because I regret it.","I'm sorry because I hurt you, and you deserved better from me.",{"type":"heading","text":"The Morning I Had to Leave 🥹"},"Morning came, and I had a flight to catch that day.","We had been planning to check out and leave in the morning, but everything felt different now.","Gyanvee was disappointed with me. She was questioning why she had trusted me, and I could see that our time together had been overshadowed by what I had done.","I was hurting too, but I knew I couldn't make my pain the centre of the situation. I was the one who had hurt her, and she had every right to feel what she felt.","I wanted to make things better, but I also knew that I couldn't demand that she feel okay just because I was sorry.","Eventually, it was time to leave.","I dropped her at the auto stand.","And then we went our separate ways.","She had to return to her world in Etawah, and I had to begin my journey back to Pune. I took a bus from Etawah to Lucknow and continued towards my flight.","As I travelled, I had so much to think about.","I had finally met the girl I had spent months dreaming of meeting. I had seen her smile in person, given her gifts, hugged her, shared meals with her, and spent time beside her.","There were memories from those days that I would always hold close.","But there was also pain—pain I had caused, regret I couldn't simply switch off, and trust that I knew I had damaged.","I had spent so long thinking about how to reach her that I hadn't fully understood how much responsibility came with being someone she trusted.","I wanted to be a good boyfriend. I wanted to make her happy. I wanted to be someone she could feel safe with.","But wanting to be that person wasn't enough.","I had to act like that person, especially when it mattered most.",{"type":"heading","text":"The Memory That Changed Everything ❤️‍🩹"},"When I look back at that trip, I remember the boy who was terrified of missing his flight because he thought he might lose his chance to meet the girl he loved.","I remember the auto ride, the nervous silence, the terrible opening line, the bouquet, the studs, and the first hug.","I remember the silly movie conversation, the laughter with Ariba, and the feeling of finally being in the same place as Gyanvee after so many months apart.","Those moments are real, and they matter to me.","But so does the hurt I caused.","I can't tell this story honestly if I keep only the beautiful parts and hide the moments when I failed her.","Love is not proved by how far you travel, how many plans you make, or how desperately you want to see someone.","It is also shown through respect, patience, honesty, and the ability to take responsibility when you make a mistake.","I wish I had understood that more deeply then.","Gyanvee, our first meeting gave me some of the memories I had dreamed of for so long. But it also gave me a painful lesson about the kind of partner I needed to become.","I cannot ask the past to change.","All I can do is be honest about it, learn from it, and make sure my actions—not just my words—reflect what I say I have learned.","You deserved to feel safe with me, and I am sorry for the time I failed to give you that.","This chapter isn't the perfect love story I once imagined writing.","It's our story as it happened: beautiful in some moments, painful in others, and real enough to teach me that loving someone means taking responsibility for the way you treat them.","And that is the truth I want to carry forward. ❤️‍🩹"]},{"title":"Loving Her, But Failing to Understand Her ❤️‍🩹","subtitle":"Pune & Etawah — two cities, one troubled relationship","paragraphs":["I was back in Pune, and Gyanvee was in Etawah.","We were back to our long-distance relationship, but this time, things were different.","Before meeting her, I used to count the days until I could finally see her. Now that we had met, I wanted nothing more than to make her happy and somehow make up for the hurt I had caused.","But instead of making things better, I kept making them worse.","Daily fights had started between us, and most of the time, I knew I was the one making mistakes. The worst part was that even when I realised something was wrong, I didn't know how to handle it properly.","Instead of sitting with the problem and helping her through it, I would try to run away from the situation.","How chutiya I was. 🥲","I wanted my baby to be happy. I wanted her to smile when she talked to me, to feel loved, and to sleep peacefully at night.","But my actions were giving her the opposite.","She was frustrated. She was stressed. Sometimes, she couldn't even sleep properly at night because of everything that was happening between us.","And there I was, the same boy who claimed that she was his priority, repeatedly doing things that made her feel otherwise.","She would give me clues about what was bothering her. Sometimes, she would try to explain things indirectly, hoping I would understand.","But I didn't.","I kept misunderstanding her feelings. I kept making mistakes on top of mistakes, and she kept getting hurt.","I was worried about her. I genuinely didn't want my baby to be in that condition. But I didn't know how to help her, and in trying to fix everything my own way, I often made things worse.","Sometimes, she would cry because of me.","And honestly, that was one of the most embarrassing feelings for me—not because I was embarrassed by her tears, but because someone who loved me so much was crying because of the way I treated her.","She trusted me. She wanted me to understand her.","And I kept failing to do that.","I wish I could go back and tell my younger self one simple thing:","Bhai, not every problem needs an argument, an explanation, or an escape route. Sometimes, your girl just needs you to listen and understand why she's hurting.","But back then, I was still learning that the hard way.",{"type":"heading","text":"The Day She Finally Explained Her Fear 🥹"},"There was something Gyanvee was scared of, something I hadn't properly understood even though she had given me so many clues.","I was so busy trying to make things work according to my own understanding that I wasn't paying enough attention to what she was actually feeling.","Then one day, she finally explained what she had been afraid of.","And suddenly, things started making more sense.","I tried to console her. I told her I would always be there for her, that she didn't have to face everything alone.","Even then, a part of me knew that I hadn't always acted like someone she could depend on.","After the mistakes I had made, I didn't feel I had earned the right to expect her to treat me as though nothing had happened.","But I wanted to do better.","I wanted her to feel that I was listening now, that I was finally trying to understand instead of simply reacting.","Slowly, things between us started improving.","The fights became less frequent, and we began finding our way back to each other. She started moving forward from what had happened, and we were finally at a better stage again.","I was relieved.","I didn't want us to keep hurting each other. I wanted us to have the kind of relationship where we could talk openly, understand each other, and feel safe sharing our fears.","For the first time in a while, it felt as though we were getting somewhere.","And then July arrived.","The Next Plan: Bring My Baby to Pune! ❤️✈️","With things getting better between us, my mind immediately started making new plans.","This time, I wanted Gyanvee to come to Pune.","I imagined taking her on bike rides, exploring cafés, visiting clubs, and showing her around the city. I wanted to spend proper time with her, create new memories, and give us something happy to look forward to.","So I asked her to come to Pune towards the end of July.","But there was a problem.","Her external exams were going on, and travelling during that period wasn't practical. We thought we might plan something after her externals, but even then, her lab exams were pending, and their dates hadn't been fixed.","Once again, our plans depended on her academic schedule.","And once again, I struggled to accept how uncertain everything was.","Gyanvee had concerns about coming to Pune because she was worried about what would happen if her brother found out. I kept suggesting different ways to make the trip possible, including ideas involving her SIM card and leaving her iPhone at college.","In my head, I was trying to solve the problem.","I thought that if we found a way around the practical difficulties, we could finally meet without worrying so much.","But I wasn't fully understanding her side.","Just because I could imagine a way to make something work didn't mean she would feel safe doing it.","There was a risk involved, and she had every reason to be cautious. I was focusing on how we could make the trip happen, while she was thinking about what could happen if things went wrong.","Looking back, I wish I had listened more and pushed less.","I wanted to be with her so badly that I sometimes forgot that she also needed to feel comfortable with the plan.","Love shouldn't feel like someone has to take a risk just to prove how much they care.","And I was still learning that.",{"type":"heading","text":"My Baby's Exams & My Prayers to God 😂🙏"},"Eventually, her exams came to an end.","And during that period, I had been doing my own little things to pray for her success.","I went to a temple once, hoping she would get good marks.","And whenever I did Surya Namaskar, I would think about her passing her exams. 😂❤️","Honestly, my baby wasn't exactly the most enthusiastic student when it came to studying.","“Padhti likhti nahi hai na, Bhagwan se hi dua maangna pada!” 😂🙏","What else could I do?","If my baby wasn't going to study enough, then apparently her boyfriend had to take responsibility for the prayers.","I was doing Surya Namaskar, visiting temples, and asking God to help her get good marks.","Somewhere in my mind, I had become her unofficial spiritual support system. 🤭","But jokes aside, I genuinely wanted her to do well. I wanted her to succeed, to feel relieved after her exams, and to have something to smile about.","And once her exams were done, my thoughts immediately returned to our next meeting.","Because now, surely, we could finally plan something.","Right?","Well… not so fast. 😂",{"type":"heading","text":"Rakshabandhan, Roommates & Another Set of Plans 🤦‍♂️❤️"},"Even after her external exams, her lab practicals were still an obstacle. The dates weren't fixed, so it was difficult to decide exactly when she could come to Pune.","We discussed whether she could visit before Rakshabandhan or after it.","I was trying to figure out the best time, and I even thought about arranging things so that she could come when my roommate was away.","But the timing wasn't in our favour.","Rakshabandhan was approaching, and people usually travel home to celebrate it with their families. My roommate had his own plans to go home, too, which made my idea difficult to arrange in the way I had imagined.","There were so many little things to consider.","Her practical exams. Her brother's concerns. The dates. My roommate. The timing.","And yet, whenever I thought about Gyanvee coming to Pune, my mind would jump straight to the fun parts.","The bike rides.","The cafés.","The exploring.","The time we would finally get to spend together without a phone screen separating us.","I was already imagining the memories before we had even finalised the dates.","That was me: a boy who could build an entire holiday in his head before getting confirmation of the first day. 😂❤️","But this time, I had another important date to think about.","August.","My baby's birthday month. 🎂💗",{"type":"heading","text":"The Birthday Dress That Refused to Cooperate 👗😂"},"I had one wish for Gyanvee's birthday.","I wanted to gift her a dress that she could wear on her birthday.","It might sound like a simple plan, but I had imagined it so many times. I wanted her to receive the dress, wear it on her special day, and feel beautiful in it.","So I asked Ariba for help.","I thought having her friend involved would make choosing the right dress easier, especially since Ariba knew Gyanvee's preferences better than I did.","And then the shopping began.","I explored different dresses, looked at options, and sent them to Ariba for her opinion.","But apparently, my fashion sense needed serious supervision. 😂","Every time I showed her another dress, I would get a response along the lines of:","“Yeh bhi nahi achha hai!” 😭😂","Another dress rejected.","Another plan destroyed.","Another small blow to my confidence as a boyfriend trying to become a fashion expert.","I kept searching, but Ariba was not impressed by most of my selections.","At this point, I was probably beginning to wonder whether I was buying a dress or applying for a job that required a degree in women's fashion.","Finally, after all that discussion, we selected one.","I was relieved. The mission had succeeded.","I placed the order and waited for my plan to come together.","But, of course, the story wasn't finished yet.","When the dress arrived, the size didn't fit properly.","And we had to return it.","My birthday-dress dream had officially collapsed. 🥲💔","I had imagined her wearing that dress on her birthday, and now the whole plan had fallen apart because of a size mismatch.","I was disappointed, but I still wanted to do something special for her.","If the dress wasn't going to work, I would find another way to make her feel loved.",{"type":"heading","text":"The Cake, The Love Card & The Blank Disaster 🎂💌"},"I changed my plan.","Instead of the dress, I decided to send Gyanvee a cake and a love card with a cute message.","I had something I wanted to tell her, and I wanted those words to reach her on her birthday.","It wasn't just about sending a gift. I wanted her to read my message and feel how special she was to me.","I was excited about it.","And then the delivery arrived.","The cake was there.","The card was there.","But the message?","Missing.","The shop had sent a blank card.","A BLANK CARD. 😭😭","All that effort to write something meaningful, all that excitement about sending her a sweet birthday surprise—and the very thing I wanted her to read wasn't even there.","I was so frustrated.","How could they do that?","The entire point of the card was the message. I wanted to express my feelings in those words, and instead, Gyanvee received an empty card.","I had tried to make her birthday special, but the delivery had ruined the part I cared about most.","I couldn't believe it.","First, the dress didn't work out. Then, the card arrived without the message.","At this point, I was probably convinced that the universe had personally decided to test my boyfriend skills. 😂🥲","Still, I hoped the other parts of the gift would make her happy.","Because, more than anything, I wanted her to feel loved on her birthday.",{"type":"heading","text":"Lucknow, Birthday Celebrations & One Worried Boy ❤️🎉"},"Gyanvee had planned to celebrate her birthday in Lucknow with her friend and Ariba's boyfriend.","Initially, she thought her brother might not allow her to go.","But, to everyone's surprise—or at least mine—he gave her permission. 😂","So she went to Lucknow, and they celebrated her birthday there.","I called her and celebrated with her too, even though we were in different places.","I was happy that she was getting to enjoy her special day.","But I also had one concern.","They were planning to drink alcohol.","And I started worrying about what would happen if Gyanvee got too intoxicated.","I kept thinking about who would take care of her if she became too drunk. I trusted Ariba, so I tried to reassure myself that she would be there for her.","After around two hours, I called Gyanvee.","No answer.","I called again, but she still didn't respond.","My mind started filling with worries.","Eventually, Ariba picked up the phone and handed it to Gyanvee.","And I could tell that my baby was very drunk.","I was worried, but the people around her were assuring me that she would be fine.","I wanted to believe them.","I trusted Ariba to look after her, and I hoped that Gyanvee would be okay.","At some point, Ariba went into a different room, and I was still left worrying from a distance.","That is one of the hardest things about long-distance relationships: sometimes, you want to be there to help someone, but all you can do is call and hope the people around them are taking good care of them.","I couldn't physically be there with her.","I couldn't check on her myself.","I couldn't do much beyond trusting that she was safe.","And I hated that feeling of helplessness.","Thankfully, by the next morning, things were okay.","They explored Lucknow, spent more time together, and eventually Gyanvee returned to her hometown.","I was relieved that she was alright.","And just like that, another little chapter of our long-distance life came to an end.",{"type":"heading","text":"The Boy Who Wanted Everything to Be Perfect ❤️‍🩹"},"When I look back at those months, I see a boy who wanted to make his girlfriend happy but didn't always know how to do it.","I wanted to meet her, so I made plans.","I wanted to make things right after hurting her, but I often struggled to understand what she needed from me.","I wanted her to visit Pune, so I kept looking for ways to make the trip happen.","I wanted to make her birthday special, so I searched for dresses, asked Ariba for help, ordered a cake, and planned a love card.","And when those plans didn't work out, I became disappointed.","But the biggest lesson wasn't about planning better.","It was about understanding that love isn't measured by how many plans you make. It's also measured by how well you listen, how much space you give someone to feel safe, and whether your actions make them feel valued.","I had spent so much time thinking about what I wanted to happen that I sometimes forgot to understand what Gyanvee was going through.","I wanted her to know she was my priority.","But saying that wasn't enough. I had to show it through the way I treated her, the time I gave her, and the way I listened when she was struggling.","I was still learning.","And I had a long way to go.","But even with the mistakes, the failed plans, the rejected dresses, and the blank birthday card, one thing remained true:","I wanted to see her happy.","I wanted to become someone who could bring peace into her life instead of adding to her worries.","I wanted to be a better partner to my baby.","And somewhere between all those mistakes and little efforts, I was beginning to understand that loving Gyanvee wasn't just about making beautiful memories with her.","It was also about becoming someone worthy of the trust she placed in me.","And I still had so much to learn. ❤️‍🩹"]},{"title":"The Boy Was Coming Back ❤️✈️","subtitle":"One boy, one surprise trip, and his baby","paragraphs":["“I Can't Wait Anymore. I Need to Meet My Baby.” 🥹❤️","I couldn't wait anymore.","I wanted to meet her. I wanted to see my Gyanvee again, and this time, I didn't want to keep waiting for the perfect plan or the perfect moment.","So, one day, I made a sudden decision and informed her…","“I'm coming to Etawah. Yes, I'm coming to Etawah!” ❤️😂","I'd booked my flight for 27th August.","And just like that, the thought of meeting my baby again started making me excited. I told Gyanvee about my plan, and she was happy too. I was finally going to meet her again!","My original plan was to celebrate Rakshabandhan at home and then travel to Etawah once she returned to college after visiting her home. I wanted to plan everything properly so that I could spend time with her.","But there was one thing that hurt me more than I could explain.","I wanted to be with her on her birthday.","I wanted to make all the plans myself. I wanted to decide what we would do, where we would go, and how I would make her feel special. I wanted to be the one standing beside her on her special day, making memories that would belong to us.","But because of changes in my team at work, I couldn't take leave for her birthday. I had KT and demo sessions, and my plans fell apart.","It genuinely hurt me.","Someone else was making plans for my Gyanvee. Someone else would be there to celebrate with her, while I would be far away, wishing I could be there too.","Why are they making plans for her? Why can't I be there? Why am I missing this?","These questions kept coming into my mind.","I know it might sound a little selfish, but I wanted to do those things for her myself. I wanted to see her smile because of something I'd planned. I wanted to be there to make her birthday special.","But even though I was hurting, there was another part of me that wanted her to enjoy every moment.","If I couldn't be there, at least I wanted my baby to be happy.","And that was what mattered most. ❤️",{"type":"heading","text":"The Boy Who Suddenly Became a Shayar 😂🌹"},"For a couple of days, I even became a shayar for her.","Now, let's be honest. I wasn't particularly good at shayari. 😂 But when it comes to Gyanvee, this boy was always ready to try something new.","I searched for shayaris on Google, memorised a few, and recited them to her during our calls.","And the best part?","She was happy. ☺️❤️","That was enough for me.","I didn't need to be a professional poet. I just wanted to do little things that could make her smile. Even if the words weren't originally mine, the feelings behind my efforts were genuine.","And then there was the song.","There was a song I'd been listening to since the time I started talking to her — Sitaare from the movie Ikkis. I don't know how to explain it, but some songs become connected to a person without us even realising when it happens.","For me, this song became connected to Gyanvee.","There was another song I thought about singing to her: Toota Jo Kabhi Tara. Some of its lines always reminded me of her.","“Hmm, maine suni hai pariyon ki kahani…”","“Vaisa hi noor tera chehra hai, tera ruhani…”","“Aa tujhko main apni, aa ja meri baahon mein chhupa loon…”","“Hmm, apni iss zameen ko kar doon main aasmaani…”","Gyanvee, I don't think I'll ever be able to describe properly what these lines make me feel.","Whenever I hear them, they remind me of you. They bring back those feelings, those memories, and that strange happiness that I can't explain in words.","Even today, I feel like these lines will always remind me of you. They give me goosebumps because, somewhere along the way, a song became more than just a song.","It became a little piece of my memories with you. ❤️🥹","And, of course, I couldn't just sing it casually. I had to make a whole project out of it. 😂","My throat wasn't in good condition at that time. So I drank lots of warm water and even tried laung (cloves), hoping my voice would somehow become better.","I tried and tried because I wanted to sing it for her.","And finally, I sang it.","Was it good?","Well… let's just say I tried my best. 🥲😂","But honestly, I don't think the important part was how well I sang. I wanted her to hear the song through my voice and understand why it reminded me of her.","That was my little effort for my baby. ❤️",{"type":"heading","text":"From Home to Etawah ❤️✈️"},"Eventually, I reached home.","Now the next task was to figure out our stay. We discussed whether we should stay in Etawah or Lucknow. After thinking about it, we decided to spend the first few days in Etawah and then stay in Lucknow for another two or three days.","The plan was finally taking shape.","I celebrated Rakshabandhan at home, while Gyanvee returned to Etawah with her friend Ariba, who had joined her from Lucknow.","And then came my turn to leave.","I told my family that I was going on a trip with my friends.","Ah, the things people do to meet the person they love! 😂❤️","Sometimes, meeting someone special requires so much planning that the trip itself starts feeling like a secret mission.","And now, this boy was officially on his way to meet his baby again.","I left home and travelled to Lucknow, where I stayed at my friend's flat for the night. The next morning, I left for Etawah.","I was so excited.","I was going to see Gyanvee again!","The thought kept running through my mind. I couldn't wait to be around her, talk to her face to face, and make more memories together.","Finally, I reached Etawah.","It was around 11 a.m.","And guess what?","I hadn't called her yet. 😂","I thought she might still be sleeping, so I decided not to disturb her. I waited, imagining that I'd let her rest a little longer before telling her I had arrived.","Then, around noon, my phone rang.","It was Gyanvee.","She asked me whether I'd left for Etawah yet.","And I casually told her that I was already there.","She scolded me! 😂❤️","She asked why I hadn't called her.","I explained that I thought she might be sleeping and I didn't want to disturb her.","But, well, apparently, my baby didn't appreciate my brilliant plan of letting her sleep without informing her that I'd arrived in her city. 😂","And honestly, I could understand her point. I'd travelled all that way to meet her, and she wanted to know when I was coming.","I was already in Etawah, waiting for the moment when I'd see her again.","And now she knew it too.",{"type":"heading","text":"Here We Go Again, My Baby ❤️🥹"},"And just like that, I was back in Etawah.","The same city where I'd met her for the first time. The same city that held memories I would never forget.","But this time, I wasn't a stranger travelling to meet a girl for the first time.","This time, I was going back to meet my Gyanvee.","The girl who had become such a big part of my everyday life. The girl whose smile could make me happy, whose words could make me nervous, and whose presence meant more to me than I could explain.","I was excited all over again.","A little nervous, too, perhaps. Because no matter how many times you talk to someone, the thought of seeing them again can still make your heart race.","I had travelled all this way because I wanted to be with her.","And now, the moment was getting closer.","The boy was in Etawah again. And this time, he was going to meet his baby once more. ❤️🌹"]},{"title":"More Memories, More Love, and Another Goodbye ❤️🥹","subtitle":"More memories, more love, and another goodbye","paragraphs":[{"type":"heading","text":"Meeting My Baby Again ❤️🌹"},"The moment had finally arrived again.","I left the hotel room and took an auto towards Gyanvee's college. This time, finding an auto in Etawah was much easier than it had been during my first visit. 😂","As I headed towards her, I felt less nervous than I had the first time. I was still excited, of course, but now I knew what it felt like to be around her. I wasn't going to meet a stranger anymore.","I was going to meet my baby again. ☺️❤️","When I reached her college, I asked the auto driver to stop in front of her hostel gate.","And there she was.","Gyanvee was walking towards me with a bag in her hand.","This time, she hugged me.","SHE HUGGED ME FIRST! 🥹❤️","I was a little shy, but inside, I was so happy. I had missed her, and getting that hug felt wonderful.",{"type":"heading","text":"Then she handed me her bag and said,"},"“Pakdo isse.” 😂","I know, I know! I should have taken the bag from her myself. I should have been more attentive.","But what could I do? The moment she hugged me, my brain stopped working again. 😂❤️","Sorry, Gyanvee. Agli baar thoda smart banne ki koshish karunga! 🤭",{"type":"heading","text":"The Auto Ride and Those Cute Little Hands ☺️❤️"},"This time, we were sitting together in the auto, and I wasn't nearly as shy as I had been during our first meeting.","I could look at her properly.","And honestly, she looked so cute. ☺️❤️","I kept looking at her, thinking how badly I wanted to pinch her cheeks and pull them a little. I wanted to hug her again, too, but the auto driver was busy driving us towards our destination. 😂","I even wanted to hold her hand, but for some reason, I was still a little scared to do it directly.","So, naturally, my brilliant brain came up with an excuse.",{"type":"heading","text":"I said something like,"},"“Laao, tumhare haath ki lakeerein dekhta hoon.” 🤭❤️","And there I was, looking for an excuse to hold her hand!","I thought she had understood what I was trying to do. But honestly, I was so busy admiring her that I couldn't stop looking at her.","And do you know what made her look even cuter?","She had tied her hair.","I'd told her earlier that I liked her hair tied up, and she remembered that.","Maybe it was a small thing, but it made me happy. It felt special when the person you love remembers the little things you like.","We talked throughout the ride, and soon, we reached our room.","Our time together had officially begun. ❤️",{"type":"heading","text":"Lunch, Judging Uncles, and Our Little World 😂🍽️"},"After settling in, we went to a restaurant for lunch.","And I still remember how we were surrounded by buddhe uncles. 😂","I felt as if everyone was judging us!","Maybe they were. Maybe they weren't. But at that moment, we didn't care.","We were together, enjoying our lunch and our time with each other. And that was enough.","Gyanvee was happy, I was happy, and for a little while, the rest of the world didn't matter.","After lunch, we returned to the room and started watching a movie on my phone.","We were sitting on the bed, and I hugged her.","And then there was her smell.","Gyanvee, I don't know how to describe it, but there was something about your fragrance that stayed with me. It was one of those little details I felt I could never forget.","I was holding you close, feeling happy just to have you beside me again.","I wanted to kiss you, but this time, I was scared because of what had happened during our previous visit.","I didn't want to repeat my mistakes.",{"type":"heading","text":"Even Gyanvee noticed how cautious I was and joked,"},"“Poora darr ka mahaul hai na!” 😂",{"type":"heading","text":"I replied,"},"“Nahi, aisa nahi hai!” 😂","But the truth?","I was genuinely scared. 😂","I was trying to be careful, and I knew that respecting her comfort mattered more than rushing into anything.","Still, the way she teased me about it made the moment funny.","And that was us: a little romance, a little awkwardness, and plenty of teasing. ❤️",{"type":"heading","text":"A Ring, a Proposal, and a Little Surprise 💍❤️"},"Later, I suggested that we could have some drinks together, and she agreed.","I went out and bought the drinks, along with peanuts, chakna, and a few other things.","There was also something else I had planned for her, but…","Sorry, Gyanvee. Gussa mat hona! 🤭😂❤️","Anyway, we started drinking, and after a while, I told her that I had something for her.","I asked her to guess what it was.","And then I took out a ring.","Yes, a ring! 💍❤️","I had actually wanted to propose to her in a unique way. I had imagined planning something special, something she would remember forever.","But I hadn't found the right opportunity for the kind of proposal I had imagined.","And somehow, in that moment, with her right there beside me, it felt like the perfect time to do it.","So I proposed to her.","And, of course, I had to add my own little dialogue.","“Ab mat bolna commitment nahi hai!” 😂❤️","That was my way of teasing her while making my feelings clear.","It wasn't some grand proposal with a beautifully decorated room or an elaborate plan. It was our moment, in our own little way.","We kissed, spent the night together, and made another memory that would always be part of our story.","This time, I wasn't just thinking about when I would get to meet her again.","I was happy that she was there with me, wearing the ring I'd given her.","And for that moment, everything felt beautiful. ❤️🥹","The Next Morning: Hangovers and Terrible Biryani 😂","The next day began with hangovers.","Romantic stories never tell you enough about the morning after a night of drinking. 😂","We eventually got ready and went out for lunch.","I ordered vegetable biryani.","And honestly?","It was awful. 🥲😂","But we'd ordered it, so we had to eat it!","Sometimes, memories aren't made from perfect meals or perfect plans. Sometimes, they're made from sitting together, eating terrible food, and laughing about it afterwards.","That was another little moment with my baby.","Later, we decided that we would head to Lucknow that day.","There was an issue involving her phone, so I'd brought a spare phone. We changed the SIM cards, and I dropped her phone off at her college for Ariba.","After that, I returned to the room.","And then came another memory from our time together.",{"type":"heading","text":"Our Little Conversations Became Realities 🤭❤️"},"Gyanvee and I used to have all kinds of conversations on calls.","Sometimes, we'd talk about things we wanted to do together someday. Sometimes, we'd make up stories at night, creating characters based on ourselves and imagining different situations.","We also used to joke and talk about taking a shower together.","It was one of those naughty conversations that made us laugh and blush, even though we were far apart.","And now, we were together again.","We took a shower together, something we'd talked about before.","Afterwards, we got ready and went to a restaurant.","This time, we found a cosy place to sit, and the atmosphere felt lovely.","I think this was probably one of our first proper dates.","There was even a birthday party happening nearby, and we spent some time making fun of the uncles and aunties around us. 😂","We were just enjoying ourselves, laughing at little things, and being silly together.","It was a good night out.","And I was happy because I was getting to experience all these ordinary little moments with her, not just talking about them over the phone.","Later, we returned to our room.","Remember those roleplay stories we used to discuss on calls?","Well, we decided to try one in real life.","And let's just say…","Being an actor is much harder than it looks! 😂😂","We couldn't take it seriously for very long. It was difficult to stay in character, and the whole thing became funny in its own way.","But that's what made it special.","We weren't trying to create a perfect romantic movie scene. We were just two people trying something new together and laughing at how awkward we could be.","And honestly, I loved those little moments. ❤️",{"type":"heading","text":"Goodbye to Etawah, Hello to Lucknow 🚆❤️"},"The next day, we headed towards the station to catch a train to Lucknow.","And there, I discovered something wonderful.","Ghoda chai! ☕😂","We had breakfast, and we ordered chai and Bun.","Gyanvee, that breakfast was genuinely good!","I think it was one of the best breakfasts I'd had in months. Maybe the food really was that good, or maybe sharing it with you made everything taste better.","Either way, it became another lovely memory.","After breakfast, we boarded the train and headed to Lucknow.","A new city, more time together, and more memories waiting to happen.","I couldn't have asked for much more at that moment. ❤️",{"type":"heading","text":"My Baby in My Lap 🥹❤️"},"Once we reached Lucknow, I booked a one-bedroom flat for us.","We settled in, and at one point, Gyanvee was sitting on my lap while I was on the sofa.","I can't explain how happy that made me.","My baby was sitting in my lap.","It sounds like such a simple thing, doesn't it?","But sometimes, the smallest moments become the ones you want to hold on to forever.","After spending so much time apart, talking through phone screens and missing each other, having her right there with me felt special.","I just wanted to stay in that moment a little longer.","We had plans to go clubbing, but it was a weekday, so we thought there might not be much of a crowd.","I rented an Activa for us.","It wasn't our first scooter ride together, but I still had a little dream in my mind.","I wanted her to sit on my bike someday.","For that, though, she would have to come to Pune. ❤️","Maybe one day, I thought.","Maybe one day, we'll have more opportunities to do all these little things without having to plan every moment around distance, work, college, and everything else.","For now, I was happy with the memories we were making.",{"type":"heading","text":"Clock Tower, a Café, and the Missing Dessert 🍰😂"},"We went to the Clock Tower area and visited a café.","There was a rush, and finding a table wasn't easy.","Gyanvee wanted to sit at a particular table, but it was a table for six people, and there were only two of us. Since the restaurant was crowded, we couldn't take that table.","So we ordered our food and waited.","After eating, we'd also ordered a dessert.","Half an hour passed.","No dessert.","I asked the staff about it, and they told us that it wasn't available.","And just like that, our dessert plan was over. 🥲😂","At the time, we simply left.","But later, I realised something.","Gyanvee had wanted to eat that dessert. She hadn't said much because she thought I might get परेशान or stressed about it.","And I hadn't understood that she really wanted it.","I should have tried to find the same dessert somewhere else. I could have searched nearby, taken her to another place, or at least tried to make up for the disappointment.","But I didn't think of that at the time.","Sorry, Gyanvee. I didn't understand you properly that day. ❤️‍🩹","Sometimes, loving someone isn't just about remembering the big things. It's also about noticing the little things they want but don't say out loud.","I was still learning how to do that.","We returned to the room, cuddled, and fell asleep together.","Even after all the excitement of travelling around, being close to her was enough to make me happy.","The Club Night: A Promise, Some Dancing, and Lots of Drama 😂🪩","The next day, we planned to go clubbing.","I started searching for good clubs, trying to find somewhere we'd both enjoy.","But that day, I made a mistake.","I'd told Gyanvee earlier that I wouldn't smoke cigarettes, but I smoked one.","She became angry, and I felt bad because I'd broken a promise I'd made to her.","I apologised and promised her that I wouldn't smoke again.","I knew it wasn't fair to give her my word and then do something different.","After that, we went to the club.","And, well, the crowd wasn't exactly what we'd expected.","There were mostly older people around, and the dance floor was practically empty.","Gyanvee wanted to dance, but there was hardly anyone dancing.","I told her to wait a little while, hoping more people would join.","Then I suggested that she could dance near our table instead.","And she was happy. ☺️❤️","She was bhand, and I was standing there thinking…","Bas, aaj toh main gaya! 😂","I was about two and a half drinks down, but I was still on my feet.","My body wasn't feeling entirely under my control, but my mind was still focused on making sure Gyanvee was okay. I knew I had to be responsible for what I was doing, especially because she was drinking too.","Then, suddenly, she started asking for cigarettes.","I spoke to the bouncer, who helped me get some.","She smoked, and at the club, she kissed me on my lips and neck.","Gyanvee, yaad hai? 😂🤭","She wanted to go onto the dance floor, so we went there for a while.","But after some time, I felt the crowd wasn't great, and we decided to return.","By then, she was very drunk and insisted that we leave.","I picked her up in my arms and started heading out.","But she began moving her legs and protesting that she didn't want to leave! 😂","So I put her down.","She danced a little more.","Then I picked her up again and carried her outside.","And the drama continued. 😂","I was walking around with her in my arms, trying to figure out how to get us back safely. I couldn't even check my phone properly to book a cab because both my hands were occupied holding her.","Eventually, even the cab driver offered to help us because she was so drunk.","I hadn't wanted to depend on strangers. The situation felt risky, and I was worried about keeping her safe.","But sometimes, when things don't go according to plan, you have to accept help and focus on getting home safely.","Thankfully, nothing bad happened, and we reached home safely.","It was a night full of drama, laughter, worry, and memories I don't think I'll ever forget.","But it also reminded me that when we drink, we need to be careful with ourselves and each other. Making sure we both get home safely matters much more than any club plan.",{"type":"heading","text":"One More Night in Lucknow 🥹❤️"},"The third day in Lucknow was probably our last full day there.","We slept for most of it, recovering from the previous night's adventures.","Then, at night, we went to a restaurant serving Varanasi-style litti chokha.","And it was so good!","After all the clubbing, travelling, and wandering around, sitting down for a good meal together felt wonderful.","We ate, talked, and enjoyed our time.","But somewhere in the back of my mind, I knew our time together was running out.","Soon, I'd have to leave again.","And I didn't want to.","“Can We Stay One More Day?” 🥺❤️","The next morning, I was waking Gyanvee up when she asked me something that made me both happy and sad.","“Can we stay one more day?”","I wanted to say yes immediately.","Of course I wanted one more day with her!","But the flat had already been booked by someone else, so staying another day wasn't possible.","Ek aur din rukna chahti thi na, Gyanvee? 😂🤭❤️","I wanted to stay, too.","I wanted another morning with her, another meal, another little adventure, another chance to hold her close without thinking about when we'd have to say goodbye.","But sometimes, even when two people want the same thing, life doesn't make it easy.","We had to leave.","We had lunch at a restaurant, and afterwards, I dropped her off for her journey back to Etawah.","I didn't want to leave her.","I'd travelled all this way to be with her, and now I had to watch her go again.","But I knew we couldn't stay together forever just yet.","Maybe one day, things would be different.","Maybe one day, we wouldn't have to count the hours we had left together.","Maybe one day, we'd wake up in the same place without worrying about flights, train tickets, college schedules, or work.","Maybe one day, we'd be together for a lifetime.","I genuinely wish for that, Gyanvee. ❤️🥹",{"type":"heading","text":"One More Meeting Before Pune ✈️❤️"},"After dropping her off, I returned home.","But even after all those days together, I still wasn't ready to stop seeing her.","So I asked her whether we could meet again on Saturday and Sunday.","I'd already booked my flight for Monday.","At first, she insisted that we shouldn't meet again, but I requested her, and eventually, she agreed.","And just like that, I had something else to look forward to.","Another meeting with my baby!","I was excited all over again, even though I also didn't want to leave home.","Sometimes I wonder…","Can't I just stay at home forever and live with my Gyanvee? 😂❤️","Wouldn't that be wonderful?","No flights to catch, no long-distance calls, no waiting for the next holiday, no counting down the days until we could meet.","Just us.","But then reality comes knocking.","I had a job in Pune, and I had responsibilities to take care of. If my father had a big business that I could simply join, perhaps life would have been different. But that's not how things were for me.","Like so many people from middle-class families, I had responsibilities and a career to build.","I couldn't just leave everything behind.","I had to return to Pune.","And even though it hurt, I knew I had to accept that reality for now.",{"type":"heading","text":"One Last Weekend Together ❤️🥹"},"The days passed, and soon, it was time to meet Gyanvee again.","This time, her friend and her friend's boyfriend were with us.","Honestly, I hadn't really wanted to stay with them. I wanted more private time with Gyanvee, just the two of us.","But I also thought she might be happy spending time with her friends, so I agreed.","The four of us stayed together in a two-bedroom flat.","I was happy that I could see her again, but I was sad, too.","I knew that in just two days, I'd have to return to Pune.","After that, I would have to wait a long time before seeing her again.","I was trying to enjoy every moment, but the thought of leaving kept coming back to me.","Saturday: Food Valley 🍕❤️","On Saturday, we went to Food Valley in Lucknow.","We ate pizza and idli, talked, took pictures, and spent time together.","It was a good day.","There wasn't anything extraordinary about it. We were just out eating, talking, and enjoying each other's company.","But those ordinary moments were becoming some of my favourite memories.","Because when you're in a long-distance relationship, even a simple meal together can feel like something special.","You don't get to do these things whenever you want.","You don't get to say, “Let's go out for dinner tonight,” and know that you'll be sitting together a few minutes later.","You have to wait for the right day, make plans, travel, and sometimes hide your plans from everyone else.","So, when you finally get that time together, you want to make every moment count.","After our outing, we returned to the room.","And just like that, another day with my baby was coming to an end.","Sunday: Ramen and Shukla Ki Chaat 😂🍜","The next day, we went to Chopstix to try something new.","We ordered ramen.","Unfortunately, Gyanvee didn't like it much. 😂","So, naturally, we had to find something else to eat.","Our next stop was Shukla Ki Chaat.","And this is where things got interesting.","Ayush was giving compliments to the chaat, but honestly, I thought it tasted terrible! 😂😂","I don't know what Ayush was experiencing, but our taste buds were definitely not on the same page.","Still, it became another funny little memory from our time together.","Not every place we visited had amazing food. Not every plan worked out perfectly.","But we tried new things, explored different places, and laughed about the things that went wrong.","And those are the moments I want to remember.","The pizza, the idli, the disappointing ramen, the terrible chaat, the teasing, the pictures, and the conversations.","All the little things that made our time together ours. ❤️",{"type":"heading","text":"The Last Morning and Another Goodbye 💔✈️"},"Then came the morning we had to leave.","Her friends returned to their college, and I had to return to Pune.","And honestly, it was sad.","I knew it was coming. I'd known from the beginning that this trip couldn't last forever.","Still, knowing that something is going to end doesn't make saying goodbye any easier.","I'd spent all these days with Gyanvee, collecting little memories that I knew I would revisit in my mind once I was back in Pune.","And now, I was going to return to my routine.","Work, responsibilities, calls, messages, and the familiar feeling of missing her.","I was happy that we'd met so many times during this trip. I'd had moments I would remember for a long time.","But I was sad because I knew I'd have to wait again.","Wait to see her smile in front of me.","Wait to hold her hand.","Wait to hug her.","Wait to sit beside her and talk about absolutely nothing.","Wait for the next time we could be together.","I didn't want to leave her, but I knew I had to.","And so, once again, I returned to Pune.","My baby was back in her world, and I was back in mine.","The distance between us returned, too.","But the memories stayed.","The hug at her hostel gate. Her handing me the bag. The excuse I made to hold her hand. The ring and the proposal. The terrible biryani. The missing dessert. The club night. The food adventures in Lucknow. And that little moment when she asked if we could stay one more day.","All those memories were now a part of our story.","And even though I was sad, I was grateful that we had made them.","I had to leave my Gyanvee again, but I carried every little memory of her back with me. ❤️🥹","And somewhere in my heart, I was already hoping for the next time.","Because this boy still had so many memories left to make with his girl.","And I hoped that one day, all these goodbyes would finally come to an end.","One day, we wouldn't have to travel across cities just to spend a few days together.","One day, I wouldn't have to watch her leave and wonder when I'd see her again.","One day, I hoped, I'd get to stay.","With her.","For a lifetime. ❤️🌹"]},{"title":"The Boy Who Kept Making the Same Mistakes ❤️‍🩹","subtitle":"Back to Long Distance","paragraphs":["And just like that, we were back to our own places again.","I was in Pune, and Gyanvee was in Etawah.","After all those beautiful memories we had made together, I thought things would be different this time. I kept telling myself that I wouldn't make the same mistakes again. I wanted to be better for her, to understand her feelings, and to give her the love and attention she deserved.","But things weren't that simple.","Our relationship had become complicated. We had our ups and downs, and my behaviour often made things worse. Every time I promised myself that I wouldn't hurt her again, I somehow ended up doing something that hurt her even more.","And the worst part?","I kept realising my mistakes only after I had already hurt her.",{"type":"heading","text":"The Week I Forgot Someone Was Waiting for Me"},"I reached Pune on Monday.","After returning, I slowly started giving Gyanvee less time. On Wednesday, I went to watch Mirzapur. On Thursday and Friday, I was busy with my birthday celebrations, and on Saturday, I went out to see the Ganesh pandals in Pune.","I was busy enjoying myself, moving from one thing to another, without properly realising that someone was waiting for me to give her some of my time.","Someone who wanted to talk to me.","Someone who wanted to feel that she mattered to me.","Someone who had already given me so much of her time and heart.","And that someone was my baby.","Gyanvee, I am sorry. ❤️‍🩹","I should have understood that even when I was busy, I still had a responsibility to make time for you. I didn't have to spend every second on the phone, but I should have made you feel that you were important to me.","Instead, I got caught up in my own plans.","And then came Saturday night.","After returning from the mandir, I called you at around 4 a.m. Of course, you got angry. Anyone would have been upset receiving a call at that hour, especially when they were trying to sleep.","But instead of understanding why you were angry, I scolded you.","Just think about it.","I was the one who called at four in the morning, and somehow, I ended up getting angry at you.","Main kitna bada chutiya tha, yaar. 😭","I should have apologised. I should have understood your feelings. I should have realised that you had every right to be upset with me.","But I didn't.","I am sorry, baby, for being such a rascal that night. You deserved patience and understanding from me, not more reasons to feel hurt.",{"type":"heading","text":"A Lie That Made Everything Worse"},"There was something else I had done that week.","When I told you about my birthday party, I said there were only six boys there. But I didn't tell you that two girls were there as well.","I want to be honest about this, Gyanvee.","I wasn't hiding it because I had some bad intention toward those girls. But that doesn't make my lie okay.","A relationship cannot be built on lies, even when the person telling them thinks they have nothing bad to hide.","I was afraid you would get angry. I didn't want another argument between us, so I chose to hide the truth instead of being honest with you.","I thought I could avoid a difficult conversation by keeping that detail to myself.","But I was wrong.","By trying to avoid one uncomfortable moment, I created a much bigger problem for us.","And for the next two days, we argued a lot.","Those two days were difficult, but what made them worse was my own behaviour. Instead of taking responsibility for what I had done, I sometimes blamed you. I crossed limits with my words and made the situation even more painful.","I want to say something here, baby.","When I argued with you, I sometimes said things that made it seem as if I genuinely thought badly of you. But I didn't mean those things, and I don't want you to believe that those words represented what you meant to me.","You were still my cute bacchi. ❤️","The girl I cared about, the girl I wanted to make happy, the girl I kept calling my baby.","But calling you my baby meant nothing if I couldn't treat you with the kindness and respect you deserved.","You weren't asking me to be perfect. You needed me to be honest, to listen, and to understand when my actions hurt you.","And I kept failing at those things.","I am truly sorry, Gyanvee.","You didn't deserve to be blamed for the mistakes I made myself.",{"type":"heading","text":"When Things Started Getting Better Again"},"After those two difficult days, things slowly began to improve.","We started talking more normally. We began having video calls again, and for a while, things felt happy between us.","You forgave me, and I felt relieved that we could talk without arguing all the time.","I thought perhaps we were finally getting back to a better place.","But there was still something I hadn't told you.","The two girls had also been at my birthday party.","And eventually, you found out.","Maybe I could have told you myself. Maybe I should have been honest from the beginning, even if I knew you might get angry. At least then, you wouldn't have had to discover the truth later.","But I was scared.","I didn't want you to be angry with me again. I didn't want another fight. I wanted things to stay peaceful between us.","And, foolishly, I thought hiding the truth might help me keep that peace.","But you cannot protect a relationship by hiding things from the person you love.","You might avoid an argument for a little while, but you cannot build lasting trust on something untrue.","When you found out, we argued again.","And once again, instead of accepting my mistake, I started arguing with you.","Looking back, I wish I had handled everything differently. I wish I had simply told you the truth, listened to how you felt, and taken responsibility for my own choices.","I cannot change what happened, but I can acknowledge that I was wrong.","I am sorry, baby. ❤️‍🩹",{"type":"heading","text":"Small Conversations, Big Feelings"},"Eventually, things became calmer again.","We started having our little daily conversations. We talked, shared moments, and slowly found our way back to the ordinary parts of being us.","Those small conversations meant a lot to me.","Even when things were complicated, I still wanted to share my day with you. I still wanted to hear your voice, see your face on video calls, and tell you little things that happened to me.","And somewhere during this time, I decided to do something special.","I wanted to preserve our memories.","I wanted to write down our story, chapter by chapter, so that we wouldn't forget the little things that had brought us together. The first messages, the late-night calls, our meetings, our silly jokes, and all those moments that might seem ordinary to someone else but meant so much to me.","I wanted to make something cute for you.","Something you could read and smile at. Something that would remind you of our journey and how much our memories meant to me.","That was how the idea of this book began to take shape.","I started collecting our memories and turning them into a story — a story about a cute girl and her little rascal.","But even while I was planning something sweet for you, I hurt you again with my harsh words.","And that is something I cannot ignore just because I was trying to do something nice.","I could plan a beautiful surprise, write romantic words, or make something special for you. But none of those things could erase the pain caused by my behaviour.","You deserved both: the little things that made you smile and the everyday kindness that made you feel safe and loved.","I am sorry that I kept making you experience the opposite.",{"type":"heading","text":"Sorry, My Cute Bacchi ❤️‍🩹"},"Gyanvee, I don't know how many times I have said sorry to you.","And I know that saying sorry again and again doesn't automatically make things better. An apology means very little if the same behaviour keeps repeating.","I kept promising myself that I wouldn't make another mistake, but I didn't always put enough effort into changing the way I behaved. Sometimes I reacted without thinking. Sometimes I argued when I should have listened. Sometimes I became so focused on defending myself that I forgot to understand the person I was hurting.","And that person was you.","My baby, I am genuinely sorry.","When you're angry with me, I find it difficult to explain how I feel. I feel terrible knowing that my own words and actions have made you upset. I wish I could take back the moments when I made things worse instead of trying to make them right.","But I also know that my guilt cannot become another burden for you to carry. You shouldn't have to comfort me for the pain I caused you.","You have your own feelings, your own fears, and your own reasons for being hurt. You deserve the space to express them without having to worry about how I will react.","I wish I had understood that sooner.","You are my cute bacchi, but you are also a person with feelings that deserve to be respected. Loving you means remembering that even when I am upset, even when I am scared of losing you, and even when a difficult conversation makes me uncomfortable.","I cannot promise you a perfect relationship or a life without disagreements.","But I know that love needs honesty. It needs patience. It needs the courage to admit when we are wrong, and the willingness to change rather than repeat the same mistakes.","I wanted to be the boy who made you smile.","Yet, too often, I became the boy who made you cry.","And that is something I need to take responsibility for.","I am sorry, Gyanvee. Not just for the arguments, the lies, or the harsh words, but for the times I failed to understand how deeply my behaviour could hurt you.","You have been such an important part of my life, and I never wanted my actions to make you question your place in it.","I still have a lot to learn, and I know that words alone are not enough.","I need to show you through my actions that I can listen better, speak more kindly, be honest even when it is difficult, and give our relationship the care it deserves.","Because my baby, you deserve more than beautiful memories written in a book.","You deserve to feel loved in the moments when nobody is writing a story about us.","And I hope, little by little, I can become better at giving you that love. ❤️‍🩹"]}];
